  "mechanism": "repository-pinned wheel toolchain proved by a deterministic reference-render fingerprint",
  "rationale": "The repository has no container infrastructure, and a container image identity would not by itself make rendering reproducible: an image label pins an operating system, not the pixels. The Pillow wheel vendors its own FreeType and the pypdfium2 wheel vendors its own pdfium, so pinning those wheels pins the glyph rasteriser and the PDF rasteriser without consulting the host font stack at all. Canonicality is therefore measured rather than asserted: a tiny synthetic fixture is rendered and hashed, and generation refuses to run when the measured fingerprint differs.",
